{"id": "EUVD-2026-82129", "enisaUuid": "72debc74-1a9d-3b17-8446-b68f2b70e08f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/core: Fix potential use after free in ib_free_cq()\n\nWhen accessing a CQ via the netlink path the only synchronization\nmechanism for the said CQ is rdma_restrack_get().\nCurrently, rdma_restrack_del() is invoked at the end of\nib_free_cq(), which is too late, since by that point\nvendor-specific resources associated with the CQ might already be\nfreed. This can leave a short window where the CQ remains accessible\nthrough restrack, leading to a potential use-after-free.\n\nFix this by moving the rdma_restrack_del() call to be before the freeing\nof the vendor-specific resources ensuring that the CQ is removed from\nrestrack before its internal resources are released.\nThis guarantees that no new users hold references to a CQ that is in\nthe process of destruction.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:04:14", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a804b162f9bc2b38b2ed1b4752eea9faadb1645b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/91f8a17a22ab615a03743120e19935e731f28fb9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/76f2cb4f721815c3b6262a6dc2151de88646924c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b8dcca427096fc9c50f1b376847fea72bc842d31", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9abea37942534eeb049335476178696b654b000c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/43403fe45379c64fa6276e5a8ede44493e5d2d3d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/29dc2f8e1c97372c2871a70088707933515fbd5b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-92508", "GHSA-mfv8-fqx8-q27x"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0892c8b7-9c37-3add-ab97-c1dcc8fe722c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "093f87dda065e0f618dd577985eccbe85efb9b54"}, {"id": "23efbbc5-d907-3482-8bbd-2e87e7f50414", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "43d781b9fa562f0c6e50f62c870fbfeb9dc85213 <b8dcca427096fc9c50f1b376847fea72bc842d31"}, {"id": "286d9259-7341-34b1-afb8-52d4cb256ecb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7ac277a01f9017fcde4f3f81670c995992945433"}, {"id": "289b4ad8-391d-346f-ae26-69813b7de9fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "43d781b9fa562f0c6e50f62c870fbfeb9dc85213 <a804b162f9bc2b38b2ed1b4752eea9faadb1645b"}, {"id": "3ea8297d-29bc-37c5-9e77-3556aea522ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "47f09895-0e49-3cf4-84f1-4e0185303670", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "43d781b9fa562f0c6e50f62c870fbfeb9dc85213 <91f8a17a22ab615a03743120e19935e731f28fb9"}, {"id": "5f1e2c42-193c-327f-b550-1d8a2844affa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "661f9bb4-3acc-3328-b35a-4a3b1103c0cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.9.2 <5.10"}, {"id": "668b6127-a2d7-3125-99d7-5726026b8054", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "7b9e18c5-8290-38f9-b19f-6c4d3b52bb85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "43d781b9fa562f0c6e50f62c870fbfeb9dc85213 <43403fe45379c64fa6276e5a8ede44493e5d2d3d"}, {"id": "82b0236a-7205-370d-88d2-72ef9e74ee00", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "907be2ec-d067-3f78-ad2c-bad6bbb971c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.8.17 <5.9"}, {"id": "9b5cda84-7aee-3fe0-b820-35b348d04632", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "aa02abd5-8